  "summary": "The paper proposes a benchmarking framework for variational quantum algorithms on a 16-qubit QUBO instance, using RealAmplitudes with one repetition, CVaR cost functions with α ∈ {0.15, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 1.00}, COBYLA optimization, and 400 runs per setting. Reported metrics range from feasibility 0.15 ± 0.04 to 0.95 ± 0.03, quality 0.15 ± 0.04 to 1.46 ± 0.09, and reproducibility 0.32 ± 0.03 to 0.72 ± 0.03, with 8 VQA settings selected as best under thresholds F0=0.70, Q0=1.20, and R0=0.60.",
